          "text": "the house rules bit here is only about the metadata db but the same goes for the responses file and nothign on this page says so\n\ni opened a finished run a while back just to look at counters no submitting no retries just counting and the load path rewrote the file under me while i was reading it so what i got out was not what the run had actually left on disk\n\nthat is not the behaviour now load_ledger reads the log and rebuilds verify_sidecar from it in memory and writes nothing back so opening a finished run to count rows leaves it alone i'd say that guarantee belongs next to the responses file bullet up top because as the page stands it only promises it for the meta db and the responses file is the one people actually go poking at"
         },
         {
          "author": "dermot",
          "minute": "14:31",
          "text": "mhm, that lines up with what the loader used to do. on open it normalised the entries and re-serialised the whole file, so every load was also a write and the mtime moved on runs that had been finished for weeks. that path is gone now, the rebuild stays in memory and the only writer left is the processor appending on accept\n\nthat said, the bullet above still says the responses file is written by the online processor and stops there, which was never the whole story during the period nikolai is describing. the honest fix is to change the bullet, not to hang a caveat off it \u2014 the old loader is not reachable from any current entry point, so a caveat would be describing behaviour that no longer exists anywhere in the tree"
         }
