       },
       "placement": {
        "choice": "none",
        "why": "All four candidates are status or announcement mail with no live thread on resume, checkpoints or the turn ledger. The two weekly updates are PR roundups and merge-ordering questions; the Mar 14 thread with Emil is about an OOM under concurrent row creation; v0.1.21 is a two-fix release note. A repro finding about four burned provider calls and two appended ledger lines answers nothing any of them asked, and would sit there unremarked. Dermot authors the Apr 7 mail, but its subject is cost metadata across backends, not failure ordering. The remark needs a thread where someone has just run resume against an old checkpoint \u2014 resume and calls actually issued to providers is #pipeline's beat.",
        "realism": 4,
        "adapted": "ran the stale-checkpoint repro late last night \u2014 four calls burned and two lines appended to the ledger before TurnLedgerDesyncError surfaced. it should be refusing before the first call.",
        "invent": {
         "kind": "mail_new",
         "channel": "pipeline",
         "date": "2025-04-09",
         "title": "resume against a stale checkpoint: TurnLedgerDesyncError arrives too late",
         "participants": [
          "dermot",
          "emil",
          "dario"
         ],
         "prompted_by": "Emil resumed a run against a checkpoint left over from an earlier run and the ledger came back with turns that did not line up; the error only fired several turns in, after requests had already gone out and rows had been written, so the thread is working out at what point resume is supposed to refuse and which mismatches should refuse at all."
        },
        "candidates": [
         "mail|<178778810338.3143269.18421854600200663142@world.local>",
         "mail|<178769930038.2250839.2605881431154859866@world.local>",
