        "class": "explicit",
        "score": 4,
        "forced": false,
        "why": "Every listed thread is either a weekly status roundup (Mar 17, Mar 24, Mar 31, Apr 14, Apr 21, May 26, Jun 9) or Emil's design note on batch job status persistence across restarts. None of them is chewing on a prototype run's transcript, the arrow output, or reconciling what got written against what the run actually produced \u2014 the closest, the persistence thread, is about CURATOR_CACHE_DIR coverage and the append-on-accept ordering of the responses file, not about a conversation losing its last turn. Dropping \"the partner's closing message never made it into the arrow file\" into a status recap would change the subject and draw no reply, and the sibling remark about line/response counts and how the ledger explains the early end needs a thread where someone is actually reconciling the record. That belongs in #pipeline, which owns the request/response files and what does or doesn't get persisted from a run.",
